# ai-kit skill authoring

When creating or editing files under `skills/` or `agents/`:

## Invocation

- **User-invoked** (default): `disable-model-invocation: true` — human types `/name`; description is human-facing (WHAT + EN/VI invoke hints).
- **Model-invoked**: omit flag — agent auto-discovers via description (WHAT + EN/VI triggers). Use only when another skill or ambient context must reach it.

User-invoked skills cannot be fired by other skills. Delegate to model-invoked skills (`align-loop`, `domain-modeling`, `pm`, `dev`, `arch`).

Cross-skill deps: prose (`Run align-loop`, `Use arch`), not deep links into another skill's body.

Reading `CONTEXT.md` ≠ `domain-modeling`. Active glossary/ADR updates = `domain-modeling`.

## Setup dependencies (ADR-0001)

- **Hard** (`/to-prd`, `/to-issues`, `/triage`): prerequisite → `/setup` if `docs/agents/*.md` missing.
- **Soft** (`dev`, `pm`, `align-loop`, `arch`): mention glossary/ADRs optionally; no `/setup` gate.

Full reference: `docs/agents/invocation.md`, `docs/adr/0001-skill-setup-dependencies.md`.
